    skos:altLabel 'CSC'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Campbell Scientific'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A global manufacturer of environmental data loggers and data-acquisition systems, measurement and control products. It was founded in 1974 in Utah, U.S. by Eric and Evan Campbell. The first product marketed was the Model CA9 Path Averaging Laser Anemometer, which was developed for the U.S. Army, White Sands Missile Range, New Mexico.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L35::MAN0089'^^xsd:string .
